;
; REGRESSION TEST: (long long)((int)x) must preserve the LOW 32 bits of x.
;
; The `(long long)((int)v20)` cast lowers as sext i32->i64 of trunc i64->i32.
; Current isel implements this as SLL64-by-32 + SRA64-by-32 on the DR64 value
; (arithmetic sign-extend of the low half in place). That keeps the low 32 bits
; of x in the low lane after the shift pair; the high lane is the sign mask.
;
; Historical bug: an older extract path used MOVE32_DR_H after a partial
; lowering, pulling the sign mask instead of the value — (long long)((int)x)
; collapsed to 0 or -1. This test mirrors the yarpgen seed-8 shape: load a
; global i64, cast to int then back to long long, OR with another i64, return.
